{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And You</b> — the praises of Israel: the House where the Ark is, like \"the sanctuary of our God\" and \"our splendor, which our fathers praised You,\" and all this because <i>יוֹשֵׁב</i> is joined with \"praises.\" For some say: the meaning of <i>יוֹשֵׁב</i> is that You stand and sit — preceded by סלה, like <i>שׁוֹכֵן עַד</i>; like \"You, YHWH, sit forever; and You are the praises of Israel,\" like \"He is your praise\" and \"He is your Elohim.\" And some say: for You are He who is found among praises, and You are the Holy One who is praised, like \"in your midst is the Holy One.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:09.702305641Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}